Three sidebar widgets for fields that made an author type an identifier from memory, each registered in `config.widgets.widget` and usable from a block's JSON schema. `vocabularySelect` picks WHICH vocabulary (Volto's vocabulary widgets pick a term FROM one; `GET /@vocabularies` answers `{"@id", title}` while Volto's reducer reads `{token, title}`, so a built-in select aimed at the listing stores `undefined`) — it keeps the vocabulary NAME, and `vocabularyFilter` narrows the menu. `blockPicker` picks another BLOCK from `blockPathMap` and stores a field of it (`valueField`, e.g. a form question's `field_id`, which is what a rule is evaluated against — a uid would look right in the sidebar and never match), scoped by `scope` (`siblings`, `..`, a named region) and `direction` (`before`/`after`, so a rule cannot wait on an answer not yet given). `querystringSelect` picks catalog indexes from `@querystring` — `indexes: 'sortable'|'all'`, `multiple` for a chosen subset in the author's order, and an `emptyLabel` entry in single mode; unlike Volto's `query_sort_on` it dispatches `getQuerystring()` itself, so it fills up in a schema that has no `QueryWidget` beside it. Volto's `query_sort_on` and `select_querystring_field` remain the better pick for their single-index cases and are documented as such. The form and search examples use all three.
